---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field name string
---@field display_name? string Human-friendly label. Mutable, unlike name.
---@field description string What the number is, in 1-2 short sentences under 300 characters: its meaning and grain plus any inclusion or exclusion that changes it. Leave out source tables or views, lineage, column lists, and comparisons with other metrics. Never narrate the query - the definition carries the mechanics; put the query's design decisions in 'reasoning'.
---@field unit? string Unit of the result, e.g. usd, percent, cents.
---@field owner? string|distilled.Null Email of the human accountable for this metric, or null. Set it to the email of a member of this organization to reassign the metric, or to null to clear it. Changing the owner keeps the metric's approval.
---@field definition? posthog.data_catalog.UpdateDataCatalogMetricsRequestDefinitionMap|distilled.Null Machine-readable query. Omit for a name+description-only stub. Stored upgrade-canonical.
---@field source_insight_short_id? string|distilled.Null Create the metric from this insight's query (snapshotted server-side). Set to null to unlink. Mutually exclusive with definition.
---@field created_source? posthog.data_catalog.CreatedSourceEnum|string Whether a human ('user') or an agent ('ai_generated') authored this metric. * `user` - user * `ai_generated` - ai_generated
---@field ai_model? string Model that generated the metric, if AI-authored.
---@field confidence? number|distilled.Null AI author's confidence in the proposal, 0-1.
---@field reasoning? string Why the definition is shaped this way, in 1-3 short sentences. Name the main design decisions and trade-offs: the source table or view, a filter or exclusion, the grain, an approximation. Leave out the use case, who asked, run results, validation figures, and edit history.

---Machine-readable query. Omit for a name+description-only stub. Stored upgrade-canonical.
